<title>USA: BP Prudhoe Bay stake cut by Bass group.</title>
<headline>BP Prudhoe Bay stake cut by Bass group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group including Texas billionaire Robert Bass Thursday said it lowered its stake in BP Prudhoe Bay Royalty Trust to 8.7 percent or 1,854,000 units of beneficial interest.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the Bass group said it sold 215,000 units of BP Prudhoe between Jan. 30 and Feb. 11 at prices ranging from $16.90 to $18.90 per unit.</p>
<p>It previously held a 9.7 percent stake in the company.</p>
</text>
